ches:**\n   - There are 12 inches in a foot.\n   - So, \\(20\\) feet per minute is equivalent to \\(20 \\times 12\\) inches per minute.\n   \\[\n   20 \\text{ feet per minute} = 20 \\times 12 \\text{ inches per minute} = 240 \\text{ inches per minute}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert minutes to seconds:**\n   - There are 60 seconds in a minute.\n   - So, \\(240\\) inches per minute is equivalent to \\(240 \\div 60\\) inches per second.\n   \\[\n   240 \\text{ inches per minute} = 240 \\div 60 \\text{ inches per second} = 4 \\text{ inches per second}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the bicycle's speed expressed in inches per second is \\(\\boxed{4}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{4}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:598"}
